From d49fbeeab473cba701fecb489170f68d233cbb8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Wloga <michal.wloga@envirosolutions.pl>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 19:11:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] [server] Let QT_NO_GUI_THREADPOOL take effect in the
 FastCGI server

Qt 6 splits large span fills of QPainter into tasks for its GUI thread
pool. In a server that runs several FastCGI processes side by side, each
print page then costs about a thousand thread switches, and GetPrint PNG
is slower than with QGIS 3.44 and Qt 5.

Qt turns the pool off when QT_NO_GUI_THREADPOOL is set, but it reads the
variable only when the pool is first used. In qgis_mapserv that happens
during the first request, after FCGI_Accept() has replaced the process
environment with the request parameters, so the variable is never seen.

When the variable is set, use the pool once before the FastCGI loop. The
images are the same: without the pool each fill runs once over all spans.
Without the variable nothing changes.

diff --git a/src/server/qgis_map_serv.cpp b/src/server/qgis_map_serv.cpp
index ce9ff0c637..3719045ed6 100644
--- a/src/server/qgis_map_serv.cpp
+++ b/src/server/qgis_map_serv.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include "qgssettingsentry.h"
 
 #include <QFontDatabase>
+#include <QImage>
 #include <QString>
 
 #include <fcgi_stdio.h>
@@ -97,6 +98,14 @@ int main( int argc, char *argv[] )
   QFontDatabase fontDB;
 #endif
 
+  // Qt reads QT_NO_GUI_THREADPOOL when its GUI thread pool is first used, which would be during the first
+  // request, after fcgi_accept() has replaced the environment: use it once now so that the variable is seen
+  // (this conversion goes through the generic converter, which asks for the pool whatever the image size).
+  if ( qEnvironmentVariableIsSet( "QT_NO_GUI_THREADPOOL" ) )
+  {
+    QImage( 1, 1, QImage::Format_ARGB32 ).convertToFormat( QImage::Format_RGB16 );
+  }
+
   // Starts FCGI loop
   while ( fcgi_accept() >= 0 )
   {
